SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Health Plan Filings 2027
DESCRIPTION:STATE OF MAINE  \nDEPARTMENT OF PROFESSIONAL  & FINANCIAL  REG
 ULATION  \nBUREAU OF  INSURANCE  \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \nOffice Location: 7
 6 Northern Avenue\, Gardiner\, Maine 04345 \nMailing Address: 34 State Hou
 se Station\, Augusta\, Maine 04333 \nwww.maine.gov/pfr/insurance \nPhone: 
 (207) 624-8475  TTY: Please Call Maine Relay 711 Consumer Assistance: (800
 ) 300-5000 Fax: (207) 624-8599 \n \nJanet T. Mills \nGovernor \nRobert L. 
 Carey \nSuperintendent \nJoan F. Cohen \nCommissioner \nBulletin 493 \nUni
 form Deadlines for Rate\, Form\, and QHP Filings for Non-Grandfathered Ind
 ividual \nand Small Group Health Plans with Effective Dates of Coverage Du
 ring 2027 \nThe form and rate filing deadline is June 5\, 2026 for all non
 -grandfathered health plans and stand-\nalone dental plans that are subjec
 t to the Affordable Care Act (ACA) and offered with effective \ndates duri
 ng 2027 in the merged individual and small group markets. This schedule al
 lows time for \nthe Bureau of Insurance (Bureau) to tran sfer initial rate
  submissions to the Centers for Medicare \nand Medicaid Services (CMS) by 
 July 15\, 2026  and approve rates by August 14\, 2026. The \ncomplete fili
 ng will be approved no later than September 11\, 2026. No new products or 
 plans may \nbe added by a carrier after the initial submission in June unl
 ess required by the Bureau. If a plan is \nnot available statewide\, the a
 reas where the plan will be available should be specified in the initial \
 nsubmission. \nMaine continues to operate a State-Based Marketplace with C
 MS-required templates. State-specific \ntemplates will be announced by the
  Marketplace at a later date.  SERFF will continue to allow \ndirect trans
 fer of rates in the URRT to HIOS. CMS has requested separate individual an
 d small \ngroup filings\, but rates must be based on a  single risk pool c
 onsisting of the entire merged market. \nSmall group rates may be trended 
 quarterly for groups renewing/enrolling throughout the year and \nthose fa
 ctors need to be filed with the initial rate filing . The Bureau\nhttps://
 www.maine.gov/pfr/insurance/sites/maine.gov.pfr.insurance/files/inline-fil
 es/493.pdf
URL:https://www.maine.gov/pfr/insurance/sites/maine.gov.pfr.insurance/file
 s/inline-files/493.pdf
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fede8c02af10f6df@role-estate-probate.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260802T111846Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260724
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] 7/24/2026: Reminders in Preparation for Maine
  eCourts and eFiling in Hancock and Washington County Courts
DESCRIPTION:Home\nSkip to top navigation\nSkip to side navigation\nSkip to
  content\nSkip to footer\nMaine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp
 \n|\nSearch Maine.gov\nCOURT ALERTS IN EFFECT.\nSee Active Alerts\nHome\n
 →\nNews & Announcements\nReminders in Preparation for Maine eCourts and 
 eFiling in Hancock and Washington County Courts\nDate:\n7/24/2026\nOn Mond
 ay\, July 27\, 2026\, the Maine Judicial Branch is expanding Maine eCourts
  to all case types in Judicial Region 7\, comprising Hancock and Washingto
 n County Unified Criminal Dockets (UCDs)\, Hancock and Washington County S
 uperior Courts\, and Ellsworth\, Calais\, and Machias District Courts.\nAl
 l case types -- civil\, family\, juvenile and criminal cases -- will be in
 cluded in the transition from paper filing to electronic filing. As of Mon
 day\, July 27\, all mandatory electronic filers pursuant to the Maine Rule
 s of Electronic Court Systems (MRECS) will be required to eFile documents 
 in these courts. Self-represented litigants (parties who do not have attor
 neys) who file fewer than six cases in a calendar year will not be require
 d to eFile.\nCourt Closures and Emergency Filing Procedures\nTo prepare fo
 r the implementation of Maine eCourts and eFiling on July 27\, Region 7 co
 urts are operating on a modified schedule and have emergency filing proced
 ures in place. As a reminder\, Monday\, July 27th through Friday\, July 31
 st is an Administrative Week\, and all courts will be closed from 8 a.m. t
 o noon. Please refer to the schedule of closures and emergency procedures 
 during these closings:\nhttps://www.courts.maine.gov/ecourts/maine-ecourts
 -region7-notice-closures.pdf\nShareFile Discontinued in Region 7 Courts\nT
 he ShareFile platform used in Region 7 courts are now disabled for all cri
 minal\, civil violation\, and juvenile filings\, as well as GAL vouchers\,
  and attorney billing procedures\, as of 2:00 p.m. on Thursday\, July 23. 
 Starting Monday\, July 27\, attorneys must instead use eFileMaine.\nTraini
 ng Resources\nFor attorneys and staff who are new to using eFileMaine\, \n
 https://www.courts.maine.gov/news/article.html?id=13356327
URL:https://www.courts.maine.gov/news/article.html?id=13356327
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
